        \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139533679 true] [17592186246280 1113 #uuid "23875acc-b2db-580b-a704-1ad7917050ac" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246280 1138 false 13194139533679 true] [17592186246280 1145 "To find the value of $B,$ we first need to find the period of the function.\n\nThe graph shows that the function makes $3$ complete cycles on the interval $[0,2\\pi ].$ So, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/544997dc11f7c88d5aa7b3f78d8dd1059a0ac08092726983897c5992d03acf8b.png)\n\n \n\nWe know that for the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ the horizontal scaling factor is $\\frac{1}{B},$ and the period is multiplied by the scaling factor:\n\n$$\n\\text{period}=2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B}\n$$\n\nFor our function, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\pi }{3} & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B} \\\\ \\frac{2\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{B} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{1}{B} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246282 13194139533679 true] [17592186246281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533679 true] [17592186246281 1041 "field-1" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246282 13194139533679 true] [17592186246281 1110 #uuid "0f2192b5-5f17-53c9-9fe3-db2b99eca7e2" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246282 1034 "3" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533679 true] [17592186246282 1111 #uuid "79b5e06e-4a3c-55c9-95fa-e436144f813f" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246284 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1089 "q-167634" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1100 "Consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{B}+Ax,g(x)=B{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=sin⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nComplete the following facts about the function $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\infty$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $A$ is the maximum value of $h(x)=sin⁡x+1$ then $A=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933730/assets/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            If the graph above is generated by the function $y=sin⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1113 #uuid "4202f39e-d752-5bc7-9691-e451845d6a3e" 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1138 false 13194139533679 true] [17592186246283 1145 "We take the constant factor out of the integral and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{(-2+1)}}{-2+1})+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1})+C \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {x}^{-1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac